se we only  gained eight percentage points in that  15 minutes compared to before we were  gaining 12 and then shortly after this  the battery ended up dying giving us a  total capacity of 60  charge on an iphone 13  taking an hour and 20 minutes now  previously it would actually take us an  hour and 45 minutes to reach 57  charge where now it took us an hour and  15. so this thing literally charged up  the phone had a half hour faster than  before and with that instead of losing  capacity with a faster speeds that we  typically would see the efficiency also  actually increased because we hit 60  charge instead of 57 so that is actually  very impressive that means that apple  fine-tuned you know the charging  mechanism i'm not sure what else they  changed but not only do we get faster  charging speeds we also get higher  capacity so that is excellent so with  these improvements is apple's magsafe  battery pack finally worth purchasing  and the fact that you can buy one for 89  bucks now or should you pick up an  anchor and how has my experience been  well over the last nine months we have  used apple's battery pack even though i  have a lot of others i have the previous  anchor version the black one i have this  newer one that has some extra features i  have some other versions as well and  overall it has been so so i think my  favorite thing about it is just the fact  that it is very nice and slim and when  i'm charging a battery and i'm using a  pack i typically want to throw in my  pocket without having any extra cables  dangle around so it does work pretty  well for that now there have been  multiple times where i was out and i had  it connected and my battery wasn't  charging just because it was too hot  either i'm actually using it  or it's just hot outside like when we  went boating and it just flat out wasn't  charging that has not changed and that  is a bummer and that is where an anchor  will keep charging when you're gaming or  doing something else  now the other nice thing about it and i  think really the biggest selling point  is to use as an actual charger itself  because when you plug a cable into it  and you're using it to pass through  charging to your phone it will actually  output about 12 watts so instead of  buying a puck for 40 bucks for you can  buy one of these for 90 use it at your  desk you know daily to charge up your  phone at night and then when you think  you might need it you could just grab it  unplug and take it with your phone so  that is the nice thing now the other  thing that's really nice about it is  that it also charges up very fast it  takes about an hour and 15 minutes to  charge compared to three hours and 15  minutes for an or either the black  version that you can get for about 42  bucks or this new one so those are the  benefits but that's pretty much where it  stops there's been plenty of times where  i know that i want more capacity for  example we're going camping  and i will take something like an anchor  because it'll give me close to a full  charge or the other biggest downside is  the fact that it does not send power out  of that lightning port so  you just are stuck with wireless  charging which takes longer now it's you  know faster but also it takes up more  energy whereas with one of these anchors  i can easily plug in a cable plug in my  phone and get that much faster charging  with less energy loss with that i also  recharge my apple watch if i bring along  my little minimalistic charger so these  things are a lot more flexible now this  latest one that i bought for 60 bucks a  few months ago it's now selling for uh  70. so they raised the price and it's  still the same speed and everything else  like before but it has this nice little  uh flippable stand thing that is really  convenient if you want to charge and  watch a video  and it's also slimmer as well so is it  worth the extra price compared to the  black one i don't know it's up to you  but this now gives me kind of the  slimness of apple's version  but you also have a lot more flexibility  so personally i think i would not be  buying apples out instead get one of  these new anchors it just does a really  good job for what you would use one of  these for you guys let me know down  below if this is enough of an update to  make you want to buy one of these or use  it or if you just go with something else  click that circle above to subscribe  check out one of those great videos  right over there this has been max and  i'll see you in the next video  [Music]
 

